  "final_message": "Done. Summary of what's in place:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`, `backend/db.py`)\n- SQLite under `./data` (users, bearer tokens, tracks); hashed passwords via `werkzeug.security`.\n- All routes: register (201), login (200 `{\"token\"}`), `GET/POST /api/tracks` (search `q`, `page`, `page_size`, newest first \u2192 `{items,total,page,page_size}`), get/delete one (owner-only \u2192 403, 401 without token), `POST \u2026/plays` (open, increments and returns the track), health.\n- Validation with readable messages: `http`/`https` URLs only, required title, non-negative duration (accepts seconds or `3:45`).\n- Serves `frontend/dist` at `/`, with `/api/*` falling through to JSON 404.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src`)\n- Vite + React 19 + TS, Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` (only `index.css` is hand-written).\n- Auth panel (register/sign-in), signed-in username + sign-out, add-track form surfacing API errors, track list with search/paging and confirm-delete on your own tracks, fixed player bar with play/pause, seek, volume, title/artist, next/previous, and play-count posting on playback.\n\n**Fix found:** the base Dockerfile's `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` always fails \u2014 hashes in a constraints file switch pip into `--require-hashes` mode, so `requirements.txt` now carries the hash-pinned closure (kept identical to the lock); the exact Dockerfile command was verified to succeed.\n\nVerified: 51 API checks pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm ci` + `npm run build` OK, and a gunicorn smoke test (health, auth, create/search/play/delete, static assets, data persisted in `./data`).",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
